==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Etymology===
Borrowed from {{bor|en|la|quadriceps}}, literally “four-headed”, from {{affix|la|quadri-|-ceps|nocat=1}}, from {{m|la|quattuor||four}} and from {{m|la|caput||head}}.

===Noun===
{{en-noun|+|quadriceps}}

# {{lb|en|anatomy}} A [[muscle]] having four heads, especially the large [[extensor]] at the front of the thigh.

====Synonyms====
* {{l|en|quads}}

